{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","id":"pg_179889e802945b1dbf2afd78a2a9d768","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/dimitrigeelen-agentic-engineering-framework-001-vision-md-35aaaaedc1c3-fd78a2a9d768.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_f035d50335da56da8d4dae10a3e609ac"],"title":"DimitriGeelen/agentic-engineering-framework/001-Vision.md @ 35aaaaedc1c3","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_2018c6219dfb72dfd0acb9ebefb027838218775f1c7f0a1ab9d19730b0b678e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Prerequisites are bash 4.4+, git 2.20+, and python3 3.8+; PyYAML is optional (needed for fw serve and some helpers), and Node.js is optional with Python as fallback for TypeScript hooks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_250b88293dd96367dea437f48198c698874a270823a7a6962d13fd8789b0a5ff"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Approval verbs such as fw inception decide, fw arc close, and fw bvp confirm refuse to run under agent control and route to a human via the Watchtower dashboard."},{"claim_ids":["clm_42ed3a22da230600e92df9644d8e4aba2d18ddd7d1c987171fb7a92c244a3810"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Three memory layers persist across sessions: working memory in .context/working/, project memory in .context/project/, and episodic memory of completed tasks in .context/episodic/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_69d3be32c32edff26ad8273753fad67457672887423e022e93b204dd645802f2"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Framework MCP server exposes 22 capabilities (16 read-only, 6 agent-authority) to external agents; five sovereignty-bound verbs are deliberately never registered, and agent-authority tools shell out through bin/fw so the same gates fire."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9b4a532ad64f09b6efaea344345be7a19e1f23f3ecb4fac7021de4079306b1bd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework's core principle is traceability: nothing gets done without a task, with conversations, decisions, and artefacts captured in a record called the Context Fabric."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9eed03bd4cd462e36b284541bccf52cd447c1b05748aa80c398525f2dc3d9d32"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"`fw recall` searches learnings, patterns, decisions, and episodics by meaning rather than keyword, and `fw handover --commit` writes a structured handover the next session reads on start."},{"claim_ids":["clm_a703d06855b41af1fde2da0f877a5009fd53ed865795dc0dde14b0712c1c7e12"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The README states this is alpha software; multi-provider validation for Cursor, Aider, and Devin is designed but not validated, with Claude Code as the tested provider, and Watchtower auto-start is not yet shipped."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b059a7d7ed3b4f852742f9ebbdf01aa4d84bd33e8a7826e6df65d85c24f2f250"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A PreToolUse hook intercepts file modifications and refuses edits when no active task is set; build tasks with placeholder acceptance criteria are blocked (policy G-020)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba79378d9de5b1295aa6257570eb695a44253e321db25d1227ec501fa61aa929"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product exposes a `fw` CLI (about 60 verbs across 11 sections) including work-on, audit, recall, fabric blast-radius, handover, serve, tier0 approve, and mcp lifecycle commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_de5e41cb55dc06640216ad9b756eed5fce68c429f99802f8d765a5da1578f526"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A Component Fabric maps how code pieces relate, making a change's blast radius visible before the change rather than after."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e83bc772c0ce2638c050d92f148cd129ffa3c080779829852e69977d23911b75"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A tiered authority model: Tier 0 destructive commands need human approval via `fw tier0 approve`, Tier 1 edits need an active task, Tier 2 exceptions are single-use and logged, Tier 3 read-only is pre-approved."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f1ff934219c8c2b10fde5cb3797cd1c5909e737680e6e3d7a51a33eda92a447f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework wraps an external TermLink binary for cross-terminal, cross-host worker sessions, with bus manifest/read, dispatch send over SSH, and pickup verbs for coordination."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f89df1ec02466e948c27e6ae512cda5579b82e707546d9a13546668e5ab43656"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The framework coordinates agents but does not execute them; it is not an agent runtime or multi-agent pipeline, and the model lives in the user's CLI agent while governance lives here."}],"claim_ids":["clm_2018c6219dfb72dfd0acb9ebefb027838218775f1c7f0a1ab9d19730b0b678e7","clm_250b88293dd96367dea437f48198c698874a270823a7a6962d13fd8789b0a5ff","clm_42ed3a22da230600e92df9644d8e4aba2d18ddd7d1c987171fb7a92c244a3810","clm_69d3be32c32edff26ad8273753fad67457672887423e022e93b204dd645802f2","clm_9b4a532ad64f09b6efaea344345be7a19e1f23f3ecb4fac7021de4079306b1bd","clm_9eed03bd4cd462e36b284541bccf52cd447c1b05748aa80c398525f2dc3d9d32","clm_a703d06855b41af1fde2da0f877a5009fd53ed865795dc0dde14b0712c1c7e12","clm_b059a7d7ed3b4f852742f9ebbdf01aa4d84bd33e8a7826e6df65d85c24f2f250","clm_ba79378d9de5b1295aa6257570eb695a44253e321db25d1227ec501fa61aa929","clm_de5e41cb55dc06640216ad9b756eed5fce68c429f99802f8d765a5da1578f526","clm_e83bc772c0ce2638c050d92f148cd129ffa3c080779829852e69977d23911b75","clm_f1ff934219c8c2b10fde5cb3797cd1c5909e737680e6e3d7a51a33eda92a447f","clm_f89df1ec02466e948c27e6ae512cda5579b82e707546d9a13546668e5ab43656"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","created_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01","id":"pg_19a517fba4a85d87956c56eabdae3c0b","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/dimitrigeelen-agentic-engineering-framework-readme-md-35aaaaedc1c3-56eabdae3c0b.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_090e08ca26395818abfe77ae9f3d5f49"],"title":"DimitriGeelen/agentic-engineering-framework/README.md @ 35aaaaedc1c3","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:00:39Z","updated_by_operation":"op_d83603ec1c5e44eea043548f2670fe01"}
